IM178_IM326_TWMR FOUNDRY_PARENT ORIGINAL_EXECUTABLE_PARENT allocation reduction uncertainty calibration decision resilience support uncertainty evidence state report representation IM178_IM326_TWMR TWMR turns **IM-178 → IM-326** into a working target-specific state-reduction engine. Under a state
dimension budget it enumerates candidate retained-state subsets and minimizes error in the complete
past-input to protected-future-output impulse-response sequence. twmr.py ReductionResult as_dict def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any] dict[str, Any] TargetWeightedModelReducer target_sequence def target_sequence(self, horizon: int) -> np.ndarray np.ndarray evaluate_subset def evaluate_subset(self, indices: Sequence[int], horizon: int) -> tuple[float, float] tuple[float, float] reduce def reduce(self, retain_count: int, horizon: int = 20) -> ReductionResult ReductionResult energy_baseline def energy_baseline(self, retain_count: int, horizon: int = 20) -> ReductionResult ReductionResult test_twmr.py TargetWeightedModelReducer {"test_methods": 3, "relative_path": "01_INPUTS/CURRENT_PRODUCTS/IM178_IM326_TWMR"}

IM256_IM307_OTE FOUNDRY_PARENT ORIGINAL_EXECUTABLE_PARENT causal calibration transfer state report IM256_IM307_OTE OTE turns **IM-256 → IM-307** into a working target-estimation engine. It uses a compact
target-relevant representation to estimate treatment and outcome nuisance functions, cross-fits
those predictions, and solves an orthogonal residual score for the protected target. ote.py OrthogonalEstimate as_dict def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any] dict[str, Any] OrthogonalTargetEstimator fit def fit( self, representation: Sequence[Sequence[float]], treatment: Sequence[float], outcome: Sequence[float], ) -> OrthogonalEstimate OrthogonalEstimate test_ote.py OrthogonalTargetEstimator estimate_from_nuisance_predictions {"test_methods": 3, "relative_path": "01_INPUTS/CURRENT_PRODUCTS/IM256_IM307_OTE"}

